      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mountain Park began as a trading post named Burford near the Wichita Mountains in southern Oklahoma Territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Park%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office was established at Burford in 1901, shortly after the region opened for non-Indian settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Park%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After fires destroyed most wood-frame buildings along Main Street in 1906 and 1908, Mountain Park rebuilt with brick structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Park%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The local economy of Mountain Park was historically based on cotton and wheat production, as well as granite quarrying.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Park%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
